  "glossaryTerms": [
    {
      "slug": "simit-term",
      "term": "Simit",
      "definition": "A circular Turkish sesame bread ring sold by street vendors across Turkey, eaten plain or with cheese and tea."
    }
  ],
  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe makes 4 simit rings and takes 20 minutes to prepare, 60 minutes to rest and 25 minutes to bake. A simple yeasted dough is rolled into ropes, twisted into rings, dipped in a honey-water mixture and coated in sesame seeds before baking until deep golden with a chewy, dense crumb."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: toast the sesame seeds very lightly in a dry pan before coating the rings. Raw seeds taste faintly bitter on the finished simit; toasted seeds add a deep, nutty flavour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-flour",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "sesame-seeds",
              "amount": 200,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "honey",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "vegetable-oil",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "black-pepper",
              "amount": 1,
              "unit": "tsp",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make the dough: combine the flour, 1 teaspoon of instant yeast, 1 teaspoon of salt, vegetable oil and 240ml warm water in a bowl. Mix to a soft dough and knead for 8 minutes until smooth. Cover and leave to rise for 60 minutes until roughly doubled."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 200C (Fan 180C / Gas 6). Line the baking tray with baking paper."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Mix the honey with 3 tablespoons of warm water in a shallow bowl. Place the toasted sesame seeds in a separate shallow bowl or tray."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use the digital scales to divide the dough into 8 equal pieces. Roll each piece into a rope about 50cm long. Twist two ropes together, then bring the ends together and pinch firmly to form a ring."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Dip each ring in the honey-water mixture on both sides, then press into the sesame seeds, coating generously all over."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Place on the lined baking tray. Bake for 22 to 25 minutes until deep golden all over. The simit should sound hollow when tapped on the base."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Cool on a wire rack. Eat on the day of baking, ideally still slightly warm, with feta, olives or plain with tea."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Sesame seeds fall off during baking"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Press the seeds on firmly with your palms after dipping. The honey-water coating should be tacky enough to hold them; if it has dried out, dip again briefly before coating."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Rings lose their shape in the oven"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Make sure the ends of each ring are pinched together very firmly. Also twist the two ropes tightly; loose twists unravel during baking as the dough puffs."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Crust is pale rather than deep golden"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The honey in the coating is what drives the golden colour. Make sure you dip generously and coat evenly. If they are still pale at 20 minutes, raise the oven temperature by 10C for the final 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Walk through any Turkish city in the morning and you will find "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "simit-term"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "simit"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " stacked high on trays or in glass-windowed carts pushed through the streets. Istanbul alone reportedly consumes several hundred thousand simit rings every single day. The home version is a close approximation but cannot quite match the extreme crunch of the commercial versions cooked in professional deck ovens. Still, fresh from a home oven, warm and eaten with good feta and black tea, they are excellent."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}